---
// The page Paddle's domain review reads for three of its requirements at once: a clear
// description of the product, the price, and what a purchase includes. It is a page of its own
// rather than a section of the home page precisely because of that — the home page is unwritten,
// and this one needs no design decision to be finished, only facts.
//
// The tiers and their wording are the app's own (`AccountPanel.tsx`), and the price is one annual
// figure with no monthly option (#193). If either changes, both places change.
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page title="What it does, and what it costs">
  <p>
    Tidemarks is an epub reader that runs in a browser. Importing, reading, highlighting,
    note-taking, typesetting and exporting all happen on your own device — a book you open is never
    uploaded, and neither are your notes or your place in it.
  </p>
  <p>
    An account exists for one reason: to carry those things between your devices, and to let an AI
    agent read them through Tidemarks' MCP server. That half runs on a server, so that half is what
    is paid for.
  </p>

  <div class="plan">
    <h2>Reading — always free</h2>
    <p class="price">No account, no charge</p>
    <p>
      Import, read, highlight, take notes, change the typesetting and export what you have marked.
      All of it in your browser, all of it on your device. Nothing here expires and nothing here
      asks for an email address.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="plan">
    <h2>Free account</h2>
    <p class="price">No charge</p>
    <p>
      Three books sync between your devices, and a connected agent can read those three. Every other
      book stays where it is, on the device you imported it to.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="plan">
    <h2>Paid</h2>
    <p class="price">US$20 a year</p>
    <p>
      Every book syncs, with no limit on how many, and a connected agent can read all of them.
      Billed once a year; there is no monthly plan and no per-device charge. The price shown at
      checkout is what applies, and Paddle adds any sales tax, VAT or GST due where you live.
    </p>
    <p>
      The subscription renews each year until you cancel it. You can cancel at any time from
      Paddle's customer portal, and within 14 days of paying you can have the payment back — see the
      <a href="/legal/refunds">refund policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you stop paying, the server's copy of your books is kept for 24 months, and the books,
      notes and positions on your own devices are untouched.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Would rather not pay?</h2>
  <p>
    The syncing half is open source, and you can run it yourself. <a
      href="https://github.com/yurenju/tidemarks">The source and the deployment guide</a
    > are public.
  </p>

  <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
  <p>
    Tidemarks is supplied by Sad Coder, Inc., 5F., No. 50, Zhongyang 7th St., Xindian Dist., New
    Taipei City 231014, Taiwan. Payments are handled by Paddle as merchant of record; see the <a
      href="/legal/terms">terms of service</a
    >. Questions: <a href="mailto:contact@tidemarks.io">contact@tidemarks.io</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
